WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.100
What if two people had
exactly the same habit,

2
00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.860
for exactly the same number of years?

3
00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:08.960
One day, the first person decides to stop.

4
00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:10.200
And they do.

5
00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:13.930
The second keeps reaching
for it, again and again,

6
00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:17.620
while work and friends slowly
fade into the background.

7
00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:21.120
So why can one person stop,
while the other can't?

8
00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:23.160
Is it just willpower?

9
00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:27.390
In this mission, you'll learn that
harmful use and addiction are not the same

10
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:28.380
thing.

11
00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:33.110
Addiction means losing control, and
putting the habit ahead of other activities

12
00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:34.650
and obligations.

13
00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:40.100
And you'll see how comparing twins can
test whether a risk runs in families.

14
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:44.750
Your mission: work out why one
person can stop and another can't.
